      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The derivative of 2 cosh x is 2 sinh x, and the derivative of sech x is −sech x tanh x. Therefore the integral is 2 cosh x + sech x + C, option c. The example supports the rule but does not establish Math Academy's key for this question.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "correct_value": "2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C",
            "correct_option": "c",
            "value_type": "math",
            "wrong_value": null,
            "correct_keys": [],
            "wrong_keys": [],
            "ma_value": null,
            "ma_basis": "none",
