      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "Using d(csch y)/dy = −csch y coth y and d(sech y)/dy = −sech y tanh y, the two terms integrate to −2 csch y and +9 sech y. Their sum is 9 sech y −2 csch y + C, option c. No captured answer or grade establishes Math Academy's key for this question.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
