      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "Since the derivative of coth t is −csch² t, 3 csch² t integrates to −3 coth t. The constant 10 integrates to 10t. Thus the answer is −3 coth t + 10t + C, option a. The captured example supports the rule but does not establish Math Academy's key for this question.",
