      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The derivative of coth x is −csch² x, so the first term integrates to −5 coth x. The derivative of sech x is −sech x tanh x, so the second term integrates to +sech x. Thus option d is mathematically correct. No captured answer or grade establishes Math Academy's key for this question.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "correct_value": "-5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C",
            "correct_option": "d",
            "value_type": "math",
            "wrong_value": null,
