        "assets": [],
        "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199688/observations/lesson-step-33535-a0c3a55a2c36063dd2a3.html",
        "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199688/observations/lesson-step-33535-a0c3a55a2c36063dd2a3.png",
        "source_url": "https://mathacademy.com/topics/304",
        "captured_at": 1791975582.516664,
        "math_academy_id": 5371,
        "title": "Integration Using Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions",
        "content": "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nBy considering the derivatives of the hyperbolic tangent, secant, cosecant, and cotangent, we arrive at the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sech}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+C \\\\ \\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      }
    ],
